    "['ethernet jitter dest-mac [parameter1] vlan [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set services rpm probe test-1 test jitter destination-mac-address 00:00:00:00:00:02 vlan-id 2', 'parent_command': ['set services rpm probe sla1 test jitter destination-mac-address 00:00:00:00:00:02 vlan-id 2'], 'root': 'set services rpm probe sla1 test jitter destination-mac-address 00:00:00:00:00:02 vlan-id 2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration for the Cisco IP SLA Ethernet jitter command:\\n\\n##\\nset services rpm probe test-1 test jitter destination-mac-address 00:00:00:00:00:02 vlan-id 2\\nset services rpm probe test-1 test jitter probe-count 6\\nset services rpm probe test-1 test jitter probe-interval 10\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper uses RPM (Real-Time Performance Monitoring) for similar functionality to Cisco's IP SLA\\n2. The destination MAC format changes from Cisco's 0000.0000.0002 to Juniper's 00:00:00:00:00:02 format\\n3. The frequency of 10 seconds in Cisco translates to probe-interval in Juniper\\n4. Juniper requires additional parameters like probe-count (default is 1 if not specified)\", 'trans_template': 'set services rpm probe test-1 test jitter destination-mac-address 00:00:00:00:00:02 vlan-id 2'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set services rpm probe test-1 test jitter probe-count 6', 'parent_command': ['set services rpm probe sla1 test jitter destination-mac-address 00:00:00:00:00:02 vlan-id 2'], 'root': 'set services rpm probe sla1 test jitter destination-mac-address 00:00:00:00:00:02 vlan-id 2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration for the Cisco IP SLA Ethernet jitter command:\\n\\n##\\nset services rpm probe test-1 test jitter destination-mac-address 00:00:00:00:00:02 vlan-id 2\\nset services rpm probe test-1 test jitter probe-count 6\\nset services rpm probe test-1 test jitter probe-interval 10\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper uses RPM (Real-Time Performance Monitoring) for similar functionality to Cisco's IP SLA\\n2. The destination MAC format changes from Cisco's 0000.0000.0002 to Juniper's 00:00:00:00:00:02 format\\n3. The frequency of 10 seconds in Cisco translates to probe-interval in Juniper\\n4. Juniper requires additional parameters like probe-count (default is 1 if not specified)\", 'trans_template': 'set services rpm probe test-1 test jitter probe-count 6'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set services rpm probe test-1 test jitter probe-interval 10', 'parent_command': ['set services rpm probe sla1 test jitter destination-mac-address 00:00:00:00:00:02 vlan-id 2'], 'root': 'set services rpm probe sla1 test jitter destination-mac-address 00:00:00:00:00:02 vlan-id 2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration for the Cisco IP SLA Ethernet jitter command:\\n\\n##\\nset services rpm probe test-1 test jitter destination-mac-address 00:00:00:00:00:02 vlan-id 2\\nset services rpm probe test-1 test jitter probe-count 6\\nset services rpm probe test-1 test jitter probe-interval 10\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper uses RPM (Real-Time Performance Monitoring) for similar functionality to Cisco's IP SLA\\n2. The destination MAC format changes from Cisco's 0000.0000.0002 to Juniper's 00:00:00:00:00:02 format\\n3. The frequency of 10 seconds in Cisco translates to probe-interval in Juniper\\n4. Juniper requires additional parameters like probe-count (default is 1 if not specified)\", 'trans_template': 'set services rpm probe test-1 test jitter probe-interval 10'}]]": 1,
